{
 "note": "Esplanade Hotel, 30-38 Marine Terrace, Busselton (1899-1900, H. Cowell Ashton), from the Landgate aerial (Oct 2026), the street and drone photos and the inHerit record. Two-storey rendered pub with grey pedimented bays (one at the east end, a pair at the west end), ESPLANADE / HOTEL lettering on the parapet, a single-storey front infill with a row of six small street-facing gables (red-brown barges, white lattice), the beer garden behind a cream rendered fence with white palisade, the 2019 west function wing and the narrow east wing. Signs are plain lettering only, no logos. Metres: x left to right as seen from Marine Terrace (east to west), y back from the front of the infill.",
